WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.510 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the vast environments of the video game  monster hunter world are home to  incredible forms of life  from thundering behemoths  to ravenous hunters  while the game focuses on battling  monsters every creature on this  continent has a life of their own with  unique day-to-day patterns biological  intricacies and roles to play in the  larger ecosystems so for this entry into  the archive we'll show the life of this  continent in entirely new ways and bring  you closer to these creatures than ever  before and although doing field work in  this region represents a significant  risk i'm determined to document these  extreme life forms firsthand so let's  embark on this expedition together and  discover what awaits in a land of giants  on the southern shores of this enormous  continent one of the first human  settlements lies in the shadow of the  surrounding wilderness the village of  astera is walled off from the dangers of  the region's interior and will serve as  a useful base of operations for this  voyage i'm staying in an accommodation  that my host assures me is in no way a  hastily converted storage room the  ceiling doesn't seem particularly  waterproof but even in these humble  lodgings i can smell the promise of  discovery or perhaps that's the smell of  dirty laundry in either case with the  sun just beginning to rise i check my  supplies one last time and set off  towards the wilderness beyond the safety  of astera's walls  to the west the most impressive forest  on the continent awaits  this age-old environment is aptly called  the ancient forest and it is a garden of  wonders from sunlit clearings to  dizzying heights each region of the  ancient forest is an ecosystem unto  itself  beginning in a clearing along the  shoreline i find a herd of slow-moving  herbivores basking in the morning sun  these are aptanos and despite their size  they are among the gentlest species on  the continent  they spend their days grazing on  plentiful vegetation and enjoying long  sips of water from the streams that flow  through this region  indeed i find aptonoths are so  mild-mannered i can walk among them in  safety close observations reveal the  aptonauts live in multi-family units  with infant aptanos never straying too  far from the watchful eye of a parent  for the ancient forest conceals many  dangers and while aptonauts have evolved  an impressive spiked club at the end of  their tales for defense they're  creatures in this environment that might  consider even the mightiest aptonath  nothing more than an appetizer to find  such life forms i'll have to venture  deeper into the forest  at the edge of the ancient forest the  vegetation becomes thicker and the  branches cast long shadows over the  undergrowth and slinking among the  foliage is a stealthy social predator  these are jagras nimble reptilian  lifeforms whose mottled green and yellow  coloration helps them blend into their  environment relatively small by the  standards of this continent a single  jagras couldn't hold their own against  most of the creatures that live here but  like a wolf pack the jagras have solved  this problem by sticking together they  travel together hunt together and when  one of them gets a kill  they eat together while they hunt in  groups of two or three innis spoils are  split among all members of the pack and  with so many mouths the meals rarely  last  when all scraps have disappeared the  different units silently split off once  more continuing their persistent search  for unwary prey and jagras don't just  hunt on the forest floor their sinewy  bodies are perfect for prowling across  the branches above in a forest whose  branches form a network of natural  causeways an attack can truly come from  anywhere i'll have to stay on my guard  as i venture deeper into jagras  territory  peeking out from the underbrush i  glimpse the entrance to a cave that the  jagras use as a nest  and from this opening a titan emerges  this is a great jagras a well-muscled  several ton behemoth that lumbers  through the forest in search of food  while i at first assume the great jagras  to be a separate species from the  smaller jagras they're actually a highly  specialized member of the pack like a  silverback gorilla the great jagras is  bigger and heavier than the other group  members and they have to be for the  great jagras doesn't feed on small  forest life like their jagras packmates  they feed on aptonoths adult aptonos and  to take down creatures as large as  aptonoths the great jagras will need to  be quick and decisive once they catch  the scent of their quarry the great  jagras is off charging with surprising  speed  in an instant the chase is over and the  great jagras swallows their prey  whole this alarming display might seem  truly monstrous but we can find similar  behavior in various earth animals  crocodile jaws aren't wired to move  sideways so they can't chew and must  instead swallow chunks of food whole the  same is true for certain snakes which  have evolved to gulp down prey larger  than their skulls thanks to a stretchy  elastic ligament in their lower jaw bone  we can assume the great jagras have  converged on a similar jaw structure  once a great jagras has swallowed their  prey they need to make a quick exit with  a full gullet weighing them down they're  vulnerable to predation and move with  caution but eventually this great jagras  drags their way back to the safety of  the nest here the great jagras heaves up  a portion of their meal and lets out a  roar on cue the other jagras rush in and  consume the leftovers that their larger  packmate has left them this extra  nutrition will help the smaller jagras  survive this dynamic is certainly a bit  disgusting but far from unheard of in  the animal kingdom various types of  birds bring food back for their young in  a similar manner and while the great  jagras isn't the parent of the jagras  they do assume a kind of parental role  within the pack providing food and  protecting the nest against various  outside threats  but there is one life form that can slip  past the great jagras unseen the kulu  yaku is a bird-like species that is  remarkably crafty and knows all the ins  and outs of the ancient forest and most  notably the kulu yaku has memorized when  the great jagras leave the nest to hunt  which helps the kulu yaku score their  favorite food jagras eggs on earth many  generalist predators consume the eggs of  ground nesting birds to supplement their  diet but the kulu yaku isn't stealing  bird eggs but rather the eggs of a life  form many times their size so this bird  brain will need to be careful sneaking  into jagras territory the kulu yaku  pauses at the nest's entrance they know  that if they're caught in the act  they'll be in serious trouble  but fortune favors the bold descending  into the cave their prize awaits egg in  hand there's no point in hesitating  running is now the best strategy the  further they can get from the nest the  better  safe at last  holding the egg in their long forelimbs  the kulu yaku digs in this heist was  successful but the next one might not be  but the kulu yaku isn't as helpless as  they might appear when threatened the  kulu yaku will pick up a rock and use it  to fend off other life forms i learned  about this behavior when i followed one  too closely and they tried to bash me  over the head fortunately the kulu yaku  is rather cowardly and once i stood my  ground they turned away tailing them  more cautiously i noticed the kulu yaku  will also use their flexible digits to  scratch in a very human-like manner  leaving brilliant feathers behind on the  forest floor the kulu yaku might be on  the small side for this environment but  with the keen intellect they're able to  eke out a life here  yet every environment needs an apex  predator for the lower reaches of the  ancient forest that predator is the  anginath a huge bipedal hunter the  anginath can feed on just about anything  that walks upon the ground even a great  jagras is hopelessly outmatched against  the terror that is the anginath but the  anginath didn't reach the top just by  being the biggest to maintain their  status within the food web of the lower  forest this species has evolved an array  of unexpected adaptations  the engineers knows for example  is a strange fleshy appendage on the tip  of their snout that extends when  tracking prey and greatly enhances the  creature's sense of smell like the nose  of a bear the anginath snout contains  hundreds of times more scent receptors  than a human's it's an odd looking  sniffer to be sure but a highly  effective one for the anginath having  such a large nose also means a frequent  buildup of mucous which the anginath  habitually sneezes out to mark their  territory it's certainly a gross  strategy although the pungent mixture  does send an unmistakable signal to  others that this district is taken and  this isn't the only bewildering  adaptation of the anjanath when charging  into battle the anginath extends two  massive sails from their back which help  the anginath appear even larger and  these sails have another function in a  tropical climate like this one a  creature as large as an anginath is in  danger of overheating and by extending  these sails the anginath can radiate  heat outwards while lying in the shade  certain lizards like iguanas have  similar sails under their neck that help  with thermoregulation  the anginath might be formidable but  like all creatures in the ancient forest  they are more than just a monster  further to the north the forest gives  way to a shimmering seascape  along this coast a herd of castodons  stretch their legs like the aptonauts  the castadons are herbivores and have  evolved numerous defenses to survive in  this ecosystem of teeth and claws  casted on skulls possess an extremely  thick roof this allows them to charge  potential threats without fear of  injuring their skulls a behavior i  observed firsthand when i crept too  close  from a safe distance however the  kestodon herd appears remarkably  peaceful curiously male casted on skull  plates are more extravagant likely to  aid in intra-species combat battles for  dominance are a familiar sight on earth  with numerous types of animals competing  with other members of their own species  often at the risk of their own life but  based on my limited observations casted  on herds seem more diplomatic in a  biosphere of vicious competition it's  nice to see a species that's a bit more  group oriented  other species have less pleasant  dispositions in the spore-filled region  at the northeastern edge of the forest  an ill-tempered omnivore patrols their  hunting path this brightly coloured  creature is a phuket phuket and while  they are only a medium-sized organism  they have a giant trick up their sleeve  or rather in their mouth the phuket  phuket's tongue is nearly as long as the  creature themselves and can be used like  a whip to stun other life forms the  equally chromatic chameleons have a  similar tongue to body ratio and like  the pukeipuke can lash out with their  tongues with blazing speed but the puke  puke is more than a one-trick life form  during one of my many observation  sessions one specimen launched a glob of  a toxic compound quite near my head as  it turns out the puke puke is a highly  venomous species thanks in part to their  unique diet the puke puke feeds  primarily on the toxic seeds of the  plants that flourish in this region of  the forest and can turn their food into  a deadly mixture within their stomachs  on earth cinnabar moths are known to  ingest poisonous plants and convert them  into toxins of their own within their  own bodies the puke puke don't just spit  liquid venom however but can also  release a foul gas cloud that is deadly  to breathe  despite this harrowing display of power  to my surprise the tiny terror soon  retreats further observations show that  the puke phuket is the bully of the  ancient forest terrorizing small  creatures but flying away in the face of  anything that seems threatening not such  a scary life form after all  all sorts of smaller creatures inhabit  the thick and lush greenery of the low  forest living through their own daily  dramas unbeknownst to the tree shaking  titans this region is known for yet the  role these tiny critters play in the  ecosystem shouldn't be overlooked and  while there are too many to name one in  particular stands out the moss wine  these delightful creatures spend their  days sniffing out their favorite food  which in the moss wines case happens to  be mushrooms at a glance the snuffling  moss wine resemble an earth pig or wild  boar with the notable addition of a bed  of moss that seems to be growing from  the fur on their back  this coating of moss forms as a result  of the moss wine's largely inactive  lifestyle and helps them blend into the  green of the underbrush various types of  sloths can be seen with plant matter  growing on their fur for a similar  reason yet unlike the sloth the moss  wine's role in the ecosystem of the  forest they inhabit is absolutely  critical according to my research  through their natural routines the moss  wine keeps the population of fungus at a  healthy level affecting the balance of  the entire region  yet there is one life form so ravenous  they can throw the entire forest out of  balance this heavily scarred colossus is  a devil joe and they are a stranger to  the ancient forest the devil joe is a  nomadic hunter known for wandering vast  distances in search of prey their status  as a super predator allows them to  overtake the territory of organisms that  stand in their path as a result the  devil joe wreaks havoc on any ecosystem  they invade on our own planet invasive  predators like lionfish in the north  atlantic pose a similar threat organisms  adapted for one environment that moved  to another either by their own accord or  in the lionfish's case human negligence  often find themselves in an ecosystem  with prey that have no defenses against  their specific hunting strategy and the  devil joe are no different thankfully  however the devil joe seemed to be few  in number indeed with so few devil joe  on this continent many seem unhealthy  due to low genetic diversity soon the  biosphere of the forest may be free of  their influence  i've now explored the lower reaches of  the ancient forest yet there is a new  world waiting in the branches above home  to even more extreme forms of life it's  a long and dizzying climb upwards best  not to look down  while making the trek upwards i cross  paths with a seldom glimpsed wonder this  enigmatic traverser of the treetops is a  toby kadachi a stealthy loner the tobi  kadachi can move cat-like across the  branches and the toby kadachi has a  secret ability periodically the creature  will brush up against nearby objects as  a result vast amounts of static  electricity collect in the tobi  kadachi's specialized spines which they  can unleash upon any creature that  bothers them  on earth honeybees are known to beat  their wings at such a fast rate that  they generate an electrical charge which  they use to help them keep track of  which flowers they've pollinated  static electricity typically isn't  strong enough to cause much damage  however which is why hunters like the  electric catfish generate their shocks  using specialized electric organs in  considering the paralyzing power the  tobii kadachi zaps seem to have i'd  theorize that they also have some form  of internal electric organ with this  scuffle over with the tobi kadachi  retreats higher up into the canopy with  an impressive leap they return to their  nest high in the branches and stretch  out for the equivalent of an afternoon  cat nap considering the power the toby  kadachi possesses it's best to continue  on and not disturb their slumber  at long last i reached the highest point  of the forest here at the crown of the  canopy a curious environment is waiting  this large clearing is defined by  charred wood and piles of discarded  bones it almost seems like a single  giant nest  but for what  from the sky comes the answer this is a  rathalos a flying life form in the true  ruler of the ancient forest the rathalo  spends their days soaring over their  domain on vast wings occasionally  touching down to feed upon the life  forms below when a rathalos feels  challenged they will end disputes  quickly with a powerful jet of  internally produced flame  and since any given rathalos must  maintain a wide territory they've  evolved to be quite aggressive towards  intruders i think it would be wise for  me to stay out of sight yet as the sun  sets i managed to observe another side  to these widely feared creatures i watch  this rathalos preen their scales while  they sit atop their treetop throne  before curling up and going to sleep for  the night while a rathalos could  certainly spell my doom while awake this  moment of stillness helps demonstrate  that many of these organisms while  powerful aren't truly monstrous  all the same i find i can breathe easier  once i'm back in the familiar glow of  civilization the village of astera is a  welcome sight after a long and risky  expedition and despite the still-present  smell of old laundry my accommodations  have never seemed better  elsewhere on the continent there are  more fascinating regions to explore and  more extreme life forms and i'll likely  set out on another expedition soon let  me know if you like this style of video  and want to see more  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry you can lend your  support by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious  see you in the next video  you

